  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Federal contract obligations in Kentucky for FY2027 to date total $82M across 596 awards, with an average award size of $138K. Obligations are down 99.1% year over year. The Department of the Treasury, the Department of Veterans Affairs, and the Department of Justice are the largest buyers so far, obligating $39.1M, $24.8M, and $15.6M respectively. WIELAND ROLLED PRODUCTS NORTH AMERICA, LLC is the top contractor with $36M, followed by UNIVERSITY OF LOUISVILLE at $7.5M and UNITED PARCEL SERVICE CO. at $7M. Copper Rolling, Drawing, Extruding, and Alloying is the largest industry by obligations at $36M, with Colleges, Universities, and Professional Schools and Couriers and Express Delivery Services next at $7.6M and $7M. Fiscal-year comparisons show a sharp drop from prior years, where FY26 obligations were $9.5B and FY25 obligations were $10.8B; FY22 through FY24 ranged from $12.3B to $13B. Current-year totals are partial and represent fiscal year to date obligations only.",
    "sections": [
