        "heading": "How concentrated is federal spending in Kentucky right now?",
        "body": "The Department of the Treasury leads buying in Kentucky with $39.1M in obligations. The Department of Veterans Affairs and the Department of Justice follow with $24.8M and $15.6M respectively. Total obligations are $82M across 596 awards, and obligations are down 99.1% year over year."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which vendors and industries dominate FY2027 to date?",
        "body": "WIELAND ROLLED PRODUCTS NORTH AMERICA, LLC is the top vendor with $36M in obligations. The largest NAICS industry is Copper Rolling, Drawing, Extruding, and Alloying at $36M, followed by Colleges, Universities, and Professional Schools at $7.6M and Couriers and Express Delivery Services at $7M."
      }
